exports[`every branch of every billing template > canceled: service ended: website chat and phone, AT&T all calls > the words, as a snapshot 1`] = `
{
  "preheader": "Calls still pass through to your direct line until 6 December.",
  "subject": "Your healdesk service has ended",
  "text": "Your healdesk service ended on Friday 6 November, and AYA has stopped answering.

For 30 days, until Sunday 6 December, calls that still forward to us pass straight through to your direct line. Undo the forwarding before then, so callers keep reaching you directly. Follow these AT&T steps, dialling each code from the clinic's own line:

- Cancel all-call forwarding on AT&T Phone: *73#
- Cancel all-call forwarding on a traditional AT&T landline: *73
- Turn off forwarding on an AT&T mobile line: #21#

Your website chat no longer takes messages. Until you remove the healdesk snippet from your website, it asks visitors to call your practice instead.

We'll email you when your export of conversation records and the booking log is ready. Download it by Sunday 6 December.

We destroy our copies of your data within 30 days of your export being delivered, and by Thursday 4 February 2027 at the latest. Billing records are kept, as tax law requires.

—
